      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-12y+12z=-4 \\\\ 5x+16y-9z=4 \\\\ 2x+6y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
